  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1104 PM CST MON NOV 2 2026\n\nWe have a break in the rain activity for the rest of tonight into\nTuesday morning. By Tuesday, our next system approaches as a low\nmoves out of ERN Kansas across to Iowa and Michigan by Thursday.\nAs it does so, it will drag a front across much of the Gulf Coast\nStates including Central Alabama. We could see scattered\nthunderstorms with enough forcing from the front, along with\nheavy rain at times. Latest guidance looks to weaken storms as\nthey get closer Tuesday night with some of the flow potentially\nslow at times with the lower stream system. This is pointing more\ntoward heavy rain/localized flooding potential for Tuesday night\ninto Wednesday morning than severe, more so in the NW half of\nCentral Alabama. Behind it for Thursday, there will be a small\nchance for some wrap-around showers behind the front as the upper\ntrough pushes across Eastern Conus. Then on Friday a second \nfront, with a small to medium chance for a few showers with it, is\nexpected to bring down a much colder Canadian air mass to lower \nthe temperatures back into the 40s (and maybe some mid to upper \n30s) for lows for Central Alabama for this weekend into the first \npart of next week. There is a medium chance that we could see our \nfirst frost by Monday night.\n\n08",
